-- title:
--   Supersingular places in characteristic 3 have width 1
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime which is equal to $3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality. Assume $q \nmid M'$, and that there is a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $w$ be a place of the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,M'$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{jqModC}\,K$ of $j$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,M'$ of $j(M'\tau)$, which contains $K$, is not the whole field and is a principal ideal ring. Assume $w$ lies in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,K$: $w$ is rational, satisfies $\mathrm{IsAffineGeomPlace}\,K\,M'$, and its residue value $a = w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,K\,M')$ at the generator $j$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,K$. Then $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,w = 1$, i.e. the natural-number quotient of $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q\,a$ — which for $q = 3$ is $6$ if $a = 0$ and $1$ otherwise — by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,w = \mathrm{ord}_w\bigl(j - a\bigr)$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$3$ analogue of the tame width table at supersingular points: at an auxiliary level divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ every supersingular place of the modular curve of level $M'$ is totally ramified of index $6$ over $j = 0$, so that the associated width is trivial. It feeds the characteristic-$3$ cases of the stabiliser count for level automorphisms, of the node-chart description of the normal model, and of the genus comparison for the supersingular charts.
